<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henri Alexis Brialmont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a>–<a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henri Alexis Brialmont was a Belgian military engineer and general, the leading fortress designer of his age. He planned the fortifications of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> as the national redoubt and, in the 1880s, the rings of concrete forts around Liège and Namur. He also worked on defences for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. The Liège forts delayed the German advance in August 1914 before falling to heavy siege artillery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henri-alexis-brialmont.jpg" alt="Henri Alexis Brialmont" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henri_Brialmont.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
